    "H1 truth = the paper's null simulator itself (v3_across.run_null via run_suite): the 2PL truth draws each question's (a_i, b_i) from its grid posterior (posterior draws, not the posterior mode) and every dataset has the 391 observed split columns, each conditioned on being split (the paper's column-split handling); the paper's 2PL/Rasch nulls have no unparsed mask, so neither has the truth. The hostile check (scratchpad/hostile3/size2pl.py) instead drew all 500 columns unconditioned and kept the split ones.",
    "H1 calibrated p = fraction of truth datasets with p_T <= the real all-4 p_T of G1 (2000 draws); the truth p_T use 500 draws (grid 1/501). Reported for every (truth, null); the decision uses it only if FP > 0.075.",
    "H2 percentile rank of a pair-removal p_T = 100 (#{ref < p} + #{ref = p} / 2) / 190; 'exceeds the 95th percentile' = p_T > np.percentile(reference p_T, 95). A pair subset counts as 'rejecting' only with a valid null.",
